  "note": "Triennial election of the whole council, 18 seats: 39 nominated, reduced to 31 by three withdrawals and five invalid papers, so all three wards were contested. Returning officer T. G. Peel. The six Unionist nominees were returned; the three others stood \"on independent lines\". 324 voters on the list, 296 voted. The paper compares the votes with 1899 (M'Clelland \"in 1899 polled 127\"), so this is the ward called St. Mark's Ward in the 1899 report."
